TITLE: LETTERS THAT I NEVER SENT
EXT. BEDROOM - NIGHT
Neon-tinted purple and blue hues illuminate a cramped bedroom.
A young GAME DEVELOPER sits hunched over his workstation, bathed in the sharp glow of dual monitors. His fingers tap mechanically across a rainbow-backlit keyboard, tweaking 3D models and blueprint logic in a game engine.
Behind him on the bed, a serene WHITE CAT rests quietly in the dim light.
Tiredness creeps in. The developer pauses, letting out an exhausted breath. He reaches over to his phone resting on the bed.
INSERT: SMARTPHONE SCREEN
He taps the screen, unlocks it, and opens his music playlist. He selects a melancholic track—“Enakkena Yaarum Illaye.”
BACK TO SCENE
The song begins to play, soft yet heavy with emotional weight. He rubs his weary eyes, pulls on a pair of sunglasses and plugs wired earphones into his ears.
He stands up from his desk and walks over to the bed. He tenderly strokes the white cat’s fur, offering a quiet, silent farewell.
INT. HOUSE / KITCHEN - CONTINUOUS
The developer steps through the darkened living room, where the glow of a TV screen mirrors his music player.
He moves into the kitchen and opens the refrigerator door, bathing the room in harsh yellow light. Inside sit several bottles. He grabs a single bottle of cider, shuts the door, and walks toward the exit.
EXT. ALLEYWAY / STREET - NIGHT
He emerges into a narrow, dimly lit corridor outside his house. Moving with heavy, rhythmic steps, he enters the silent neighborhood street.
Parked along the curb is his black Volkswagen Polo. He unlocks the door, slides into the driver's seat with the drink in hand, and shuts the door behind him. The engine turns over with a low hum as the car pulls away into the dark.
INT./EXT. CAR - NIGHT (DRIVING)
Streetlights sweep rhythmically across his face through the windshield. Inside, the car stereo glows magenta, displaying the track info.
He grips the steering wheel, his expression stoic beneath his sunglasses. On the dashboard, the speedometer needle rises as the empty city roads blur past.
EXT. BEACH PARKING - NIGHT
The car pulls up to a deserted beachfront promenade under the distant glare of a streetlight. The engine cuts out.
He steps out of the car, gripping the glass bottle, and walks past the low stone boundary wall toward the dark expanse of sand.
EXT. BEACH SHORE - NIGHT
Darkness swallows everything except the pale foam of waves crashing relentlessly against the shore.
He sits down alone on the cool sand, earphones firmly in place, facing the vast, endless ocean. He twists the cap off his bottle and takes a slow sip, lost in thought as the sea breeze washes over him.
EXT. BEACH - DAY (FLASHBACK / VISION)
Warm daylight washes over the same shore.
He sits on the golden sand, turned toward a glowing white silhouette beside him—the ghost of the girl he loved, leaning close. A moment frozen between reality and longing.
EXT. BEACH SHORE - NIGHT
Cut back to the dark beach. He sits entirely alone.
Next to him on the sand rests the bottle and his illuminated phone screen.
